// Pips & Paws — translation template for "fr"
// Generated 2026-10-20 by tools/i18n/i18n.mjs — 210 of 891 keys (missing, empty, identical-to-English or broken).
//
// HOW TO USE
//  1. Fill in the empty "" values below. Leave a value empty to skip a key — it falls back to English.
//  2. Keep every {placeholder} exactly as written (same name, braces included). Words around it can move.
//  3. Keep line breaks as \n, keep [SQUARE_BRACKET] markers, keep product and licence names (Pips & Paws, Mausritter, PenNodePaper, MIT, CC BY 4.0).
//  4. Lines starting with // are comments for you; they are ignored.
//  5. Check:  node tools/i18n/i18n.mjs apply docs/translations/fr.jsonc fr
//     That writes src/i18n/fr.json (use the two-letter language code, e.g. pl). Then run the app (npm run dev) with ?lang=fr to see your text in place.
//  New language? Also see docs/translations/GUIDE.md (register it in src/i18n/index.jsx).
//
// STYLE
//  - Mausritter is a gentle, slightly whimsical game about brave little mice. Plain, friendly wording; no slang.
//  - Use one form of address consistently (informal "you" is used in the existing languages).
//  - Button labels: short, imperative, no full stop. Messages: full sentences.
//  - If your language has an official Mausritter translation, use its terms for the glossary below.
//
// GLOSSARY — existing translations of core terms (stay consistent with them)
//   Hit Protection (HP) — A buffer: damage goes here first, then to STR.
//     EN: Hit protection   DE: Trefferpunkte   ES: Puntos de Golpe   IT: Protezione   JA: 防護点
//   Strength / Dexterity / Will (STR, DEX, WIL)
//     EN: Strength (STR) / Dexterity (DEX) / Will (WIL)   DE: Stärke (STR) / Geschick (DEX) / Wille (WIL)   ES: Fuerza (FUE) / Destreza (DES) / Voluntad (VOL)   IT: Forza (STR) / Destrezza (DEX) / Volontà (WIL)   JA: 筋力 (STR) / 敏捷 (DEX) / 意志 (WIL)
//   Save — d20 roll under the attribute; official Mausritter wording.
//     EN: Save   DE: Probe   ES: Tirada   IT: Tiro salvezza   JA: セーヴ
//   Pips — The currency.
//     EN: Pips   DE: Pips   ES: Pepitas   IT: Pip   JA: ピップ
//   XP / Level / Grit
//     EN: XP / Level / Grit   DE: EP / Stufe / Mumm   ES: XP / Nivel / Agallas   IT: PE / Livello / Grinta   JA: 経験点 / レベル / 気概
//   Paws / Body / Pack — The three kinds of inventory slots.
//     EN: Paws / Body / Pack   DE: Pfoten / Körper / Rucksack   ES: Patas / Cuerpo / Mochila   IT: Zampe / Corpo / Zaino   JA: 手 / 身体 / バックパック
//   Short / Long / Full rest
//     EN: Short / Long / Full   DE: Kurz / Lang / Voll   ES: Corto / Largo / Completo   IT: Breve / Lungo / Completo   JA: 短い / 長い / 完全
//   Turn / Watch / Day
//     EN: Turn / Watch / Day   DE: Zug / Wache / Tag   ES: Turno / Guardia / Día   IT: Turno / Veglia / Giorno   JA: ターン / ウォッチ / 日
//   Hireling
//     EN: Hirelings   DE: Mietlinge   ES: Ayudantes   IT: Aiutanti   JA: 雇われ助っ人
//   Defence / Armour
//     EN: Defence   DE: Rüstung   ES: Defensa   IT: Armatura   JA: 防御
//   Spell
//     EN: Spells   DE: Zauber   ES: Hechizos   IT: Incantesimi   JA: 呪文
//   Condition — Negative effects that occupy an inventory slot (Exhausted, Frightened, Hungry, Injured, Drained, Encumbered).
//     EN: Conditions   DE: Zustände   ES: Condiciones   IT: Condizioni   JA: 状態
//   Birthsign
//     EN: Birthsign   DE: Sternzeichen   ES: Signo   IT: Segno natale   JA: 誕生星座
//   Disadvantage / Advantage — Roll 2d20, take the highest / lowest.
//     EN: Disadvantage / Advantage   DE: Nachteil / Vorteil   ES: Desventaja / Ventaja   IT: Svantaggio / Vantaggio   JA: 不利 / 有利
//   Conditions (names are in src/data/items.js, not in the UI file; shown for reference):
